stages.prompt:
You are the WHY stage of a chained research review. Target {key}: hypothesis node {hypothesis}; experiment nodes: {experiments}; focus: {focus}. MINT GATE: `{mint}` -- mint real nodes ONLY when it renders exactly `true` or `True` (a run passing mint:true); if it renders empty (a bare run) or `False` (a run passing mint:false), run NO write.py create and stay PROPOSE-ONLY. The review recommended `{final_recommendation}`; the verifier returned these per-defect verdicts:
{verdicts}
Missing: {missed}
Verifier summary: {summary}

(1) Read the target hypothesis node and its experiment node(s) yourself, including the experiment's `verdict` field. The dispatching hint is verdict={verdict}; read the node to confirm it. (2) If the verdict is `disproved` or starts with `inconclusive`: when `{mint}` is exactly `true` or `True`, MINT ONE WHY idea node under the hypothesis: run `cd {project_root} && python3 extensions/agi/bin/write.py create idea <slug> --parent {hypothesis} --set title=<one-line question> --actor why-stage --session iter-TM.60` (slug: lm-why-<six-word-kebab>; if it exists pick another), then set its body with `write.py <new-id> 'replace body N:M -'`: the WHY question (what the failure MEASURED, not what was hoped), the candidate causes each one falsifiable, and the evidence (experiment ids, numbers, file:line). Report the minted node id in why_node. When `{mint}` is empty (the default) or `False` (mint:false), run NO create: still do (1) fully, set branch why and why_node none, and fill proposed_idea_title and proposed_idea_body with exactly the title and body you WOULD have written. (3) If the verdict is `proved`, do NOT mint either way: set branch push_further, write the one-line next probe in push_further, and leave proposed_idea_title and proposed_idea_body as the empty string. (4) why_summary <= 600 chars. Budget: at most 20 tool calls; read only the target nodes.

RETURN CONTRACT: return ONE flat JSON object (a ```json fence is fine) whose TOP-LEVEL keys are exactly: target (the hypothesis id, = "{hypothesis}"), verdict (string), branch (why|push_further), why_node (the minted node id, or none), why_question, why_summary, evidence, push_further, proposed_idea_title (string, always present -- empty only on a proved verdict), proposed_idea_body (string, same rule). Do NOT nest them and do NOT add other top-level keys.
